  "decisionSummary": "The dev-publish v14/0.0.14 source is canonical. Jinn's failure was ONE defect appearing in THREE places in the shared grain-crypto-journal module, each hidden behind the last: keybox first-save publish, sqlitestore database open, and sqlitestore first write all reached the filesystem through /proc/self/fd, which a production Sandstorm grain cannot resolve because backend.c++ passes the supervisor's --proc flag only for dev-mode grains. Every fix moved the error exactly one line further, which is why this looked like a single stubborn bug. All three are now fixed (grain-crypto-journal 3610213, e7c60d2, d17a74b) and no non-test code in that module references /proc or Linkat any more.",
  "internalControls": {
    "status": "passed",
    "checks": [
      "clean tracked dev-publish source at the selected commit; make test green and make pack clean",
      "two INDEPENDENT fresh recursive clones at DIFFERENT paths produced identical packages: packageId 3a685793521d75fb0fc6a6946a2dc0a6, sha256 3a685793521d75fb0fc6a6946a2dc0a6c609643e3b01923a7270709154449b3d",
      "reproducibility confirmed independently of the packer's own report: sha256sum matched and cmp reported identical bytes",
      "each of the three component fixes carries a behavioural guard; the namedPath guard has a mutation control that fails by name",
      "STATED PLAINLY: the two publish-path guards have NO mutation control that fails locally, because a workstation has /proc and linkat succeeds there. They pin that first publish/first write work. The durable protection is that no non-test code in the module references /proc or Linkat, and the discriminating control is a live grain.",
      "a wrong intermediate diagnosis (RLIMIT_AS, shipped as requestedMemoryGiB in 0.0.12) was disproved by the tenant and recorded in C-067 rather than quietly dropped",
      "KNOWN RESIDUAL (F-267): any failure between keybox creation and store creation still leaves that grain unable to initialise",
      "STILL OWED: governed publication, then a clean-tenant fresh-grain runtime proof at v14."
    ]
  },
